# Auto commit and push

Whenever the user asks you to change files, after finishing those edits:

1. Stage only the files you changed for that request (not unrelated dirty files).
2. Commit with a concise message focused on why.
3. Push to the tracked remote branch (`git push`).

Do this automatically every time unless the user explicitly says not to commit or not to push.
Use a HEREDOC for the commit message. Never update git config. Never use `--no-verify` or force push unless the user asks.
If HTTPS auth fails, try the local `./.tools/gh_*/bin/gh auth setup-git` path used previously in this repo.
